From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: augenblix <info@augenblix.de>
Date: Wed, 23 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: quirks: Fix Kinara Ara-2 BAR assignment by correcting
 device class

The Kinara Ara-2 PCIe accelerator (1e58:0002) reports PCI class 0x000012
(Non-VGA unclassified device, prog-if 0x12).  The kernel's PCI resource
allocator in __dev_sort_resources() skips devices whose class >> 8 equals
PCI_CLASS_NOT_DEFINED (0x0000), which means the device's BARs are never
added to the allocation list and consequently never assigned addresses.

Fix this by adding an early PCI fixup quirk that reclassifies the device
as a Processing Accelerator (class 0x120000), which accurately describes
the device's function and allows the normal BAR assignment flow to proceed.

Without this fix, all three 64-bit prefetchable BARs (16K + 1M + 1M)
remain at address 0 and the uiodma driver fails with:
  "BAR 0: not claimed; can't enable device"

Signed-off-by: augenblix <info@augenblix.de>
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index 1234567890ab..fedcba987654 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -6200,3 +6200,17 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x9a31,
 #endif
+
+/*
+ * Kinara Ara-2 PCIe AI accelerator (1e58:0002) reports class 0x000012
+ * (Non-VGA unclassified, prog-if 0x12).  Since class >> 8 == 0x0000
+ * matches PCI_CLASS_NOT_DEFINED, __dev_sort_resources() in setup-bus.c
+ * skips the device entirely and its BARs are never assigned.
+ *
+ * Reclassify as Processing Accelerator (0x1200) so BARs get assigned
+ * normally.
+ */
+static void quirk_kinara_ara2_class(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	dev_info(&dev->dev, "Kinara Ara-2: reclassifying from 0x%06x to Processing Accelerator\n",
+		 dev->class);
+	dev->class = PCI_CLASS_ACCELERATOR_PROCESSING << 8 | (dev->class & 0xff);
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(0x1e58, 0x0002, quirk_kinara_ara2_class);
